# Accessibility

All new or modified UI must be operable without a mouse and usable with assistive technology.

## Required

- Keyboard navigation and logical tab order
- Visible focus (`focus-visible`; do not remove outlines without a replacement)
- Semantic HTML first (`button`, `a`, `label`, `table`, headings). Do not use ARIA to paper over wrong elements
- Accessible names, labels, descriptions; form controls associated with labels and errors
- Dialogs/drawers: prefer Radix Dialog/Sheet/`IpOverlayDialog` (focus trap, Escape, title). No unlabeled `fixed inset-0` overlays
- Tables: header cells, caption or `aria-label` when the purpose is not obvious
- Validation announced and visible — never hide errors
- Sufficient contrast on dashboard, IP target, counselling, auth, and portal scopes
- Screen-reader text via existing `sr-only` / visually hidden patterns; skip link `#main-content` already exists — do not remove it
- Icon-only controls need an accessible name

## Reuse

IP census keyboard helpers, `useFocusTrap`, and Radix primitives already exist — extend them rather than inventing a parallel a11y toolkit.

## Do not

Do not claim “accessible” because a role attribute was added. Do not block keyboard on custom grid cells that are the primary interaction. Kiosk/TV views still need sensible focus when they are interactive.
